​STAGE 1: Exterior Walk-Around & Body Check
​To be performed immediately upon vehicle arrival, prior to moving or lifting.

​1. Structure & Body
​[ ] Frame / Unibody: Check for severe structural rust, holes, or cracking (fails if structurally compromised).
​[ ] Fenders & Body Panels: No sharp protruding edges. Fenders must fully cover the tire tread width.  
​[ ] Bumpers: Front and rear present, securely fastened, and at legal bumper heights.
​[ ] Doors & Latches: All doors must latch tightly. Front doors must open from both inside and outside.

​2. Glazing (Glass) & Mirrors
​[ ] Windshield: No cracks greater than 6 inches inside the Critical Vision Area (the sweep of the wipers except the bottom 4 inches). No cracks intersecting another crack.
​[ ] Window Tint: Must meet Maine Title 29-A rules (minimum 35% light transmission on front side windows).
​[ ] Mirrors: Must have at least two functioning rearview mirrors (one must be the driver's side exterior).

​3. Lighting & Wipers
​[ ] Required Lamps: Check all headlights (high/low), brake lights, turn signals, hazards, taillights, and registration plate lights. (Lenses must be free of major cracks that leak white light).
​[ ] Wiper Blades: Rubber intact; must cleanly clear the windshield. Washer pump system must function. 

 
​STAGE 2: Under-Hood & Lift Inspection
​To be performed over the pit or on the lift.

​1. Braking System
​[ ] Master Cylinder: No fluid leaks. Check for pressure fade while holding pressure.
​[ ] Brake Tubing & Lines: No flaking rust, severe pitting, or bulging. No non-approved copper or compression fittings.
​[ ] Pads & Rotors: Pads must not be binding; caliper slides must not be frozen. Minimum pad thickness: _______ mm.
​[ ] Parking Brake: Must hold vehicle securely.

​2. Steering & Suspension
​[ ] Steering Linkage: Inspect tie rods, idler arms, and pitman arms for play using manufacturer specifications.  
​[ ] Power Steering: Pump and assist motors must operate correctly. No structural leaks.
​[ ] Ball Joints & Bushings: Check ball joints for vertical/horizontal play. Rubber bushings must not have excessive looseness.  
​[ ] Springs & Shocks: No broken coil springs, leaf springs, or leaking struts/shock absorbers.
​[ ] Wheel Bearings: Spin wheels to check for rough play, noise, or binding.

​3. Tires & Wheels
​[ ] Tread Depth: Must have at least 2/32 inch of tread depth in all major grooves.
​[ ] Tire Condition: No sidewall bulges, deep cuts, or exposed cords. (Adequate tire plugs are permitted).
​[ ] Wheels: No cracked rims, missing lug nuts, or severe bends.

​4. Under-Hood & Exhaust
​[ ] Exhaust System: Complete, securely mounted, and free of leaks. (Adequate welded patches and flex-pipe are permitted).
​[ ] Tailpipe: Must terminate past the passenger compartment and exit no more than 2 inches beyond the outside bumper line.
​[ ] Catalytic Converter: Mandated on all 1982 and newer models (or any vehicle originally equipped with one). Must be present and untampered with.
​[ ] Fluid Leaks: No active petroleum leaks severe enough to constitute a fire hazard.


​STAGE 3: Road Test & Dynamic Evaluation
​To be performed on public roads to verify operational safety.
​[ ] Speedometer / Odometer: Both must be operational and legible.
​[ ] Horn: Must emit a loud, clear, audible warning sound upon actuation.
​[ ] Brake Pedal Reserve: Pedal must have sufficient travel remaining when depressed fully; must not sink to the floorboards.
​[ ] Steering Lash & Tracking: No excessive play in the steering wheel; vehicle tracks straight without heavy pulling.
​[ ] Drivetrain / Transmission: Smooth engagement without slipping, binding, or severe mechanical binding noise.


​STAGE 4: Final Diagnostics & Regional Compliance
​Final electronic and emission validation before signing off.

​1. Dashboard & Electronics
​[ ] ABS Light: Must turn off after self-check. An active, illuminated ABS light is an automatic failure.
​[ ] Airbag (SRS) Light: Diagnostics light must function during key-on self-check and turn off.
​[ ] Check Engine Light (MIL): Must function properly during self-test.

​2. Cumberland County Emissions (Class E Only)
​Skip if vehicle is registered outside Cumberland County, is over 25 years old, or is an EV/Motorcycle.
​[ ] OBD-II Test: Connect scanner. Check for readiness monitors and active emissions fault codes.
​[ ] Gas Cap Test: Perform a physical gas cap pressure test to verify sealing integrity.


